WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:01.960
Water.

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:04.480
You might not see it,
but this is...

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:08.600
Here's why.

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:10.760
Every molecule of water on the Earth

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:13.320
and inside you
or any other living thing

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.760
has existed for billions of years.

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:18.520
After it came to Earth,
that water has been cycling

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:21.760
through rocks, air, animals,
plants and back again.

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:24.880
Each molecule has been
on an incredible voyage

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:26.200
before coming to you.

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:29.720
At some point, the water inside you
would have been inside dinosaurs,

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:34.560
bacteria, the oceans, storm clouds,
the polar ice caps and much more.

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:38.200
All of the water on Earth is alien.

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:40.360
They might be a familiar
part of our world,

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:43.160
but our oceans formed
hundreds of millions of years

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:45.480
after our planet took shape.

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:48.440
The water arrived on asteroids
and comets from space,

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:50.560
objects from the edge
of our solar system.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:54.080
They were leftovers of the
vast clouds of dust and rocks

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:56.040
that didn't quite
make it into planets.

00:00:56.520 --> 00:01:00.120
This is the origin of all the water
you can see on the Earth.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:04.120
Water doesn't follow the
normal rules of chemistry.

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:07.640
For a start, it shouldn't really
be a liquid on our planet.

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:10.680
A water molecule is made
from two very light atoms,

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:12.360
hydrogen and oxygen.

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:14.960
And at the temperatures and pressures
on the surface of the Earth,

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:17.680
rules of chemistry say that
water should be a gas.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:22.240
And, unlike any other chemical,
when water freezes it expands.

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:25.040
And so ice floats on water.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:26.560
Now you see this every day,

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:29.280
but take a moment to think
about how weird that is.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:33.040
Over time, this odd behaviour
has been very useful.

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:35.040
By insulating the water underneath,

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:40.480
floating ice has enabled complex life
to survive and evolve on our planet,

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:44.920
despite the many ice ages that have
frozen the Earth's surface solid.

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:48.400
And the strangeness
just goes on and on.

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:51.680
Did you know that hot water
freezes faster than cold?

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:53.280
Yes, really.

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:54.920
No-one knows why.

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:58.240
Water molecules can float upwards,
against the force of gravity.

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:00.680
That's because they love
to stick to each other.

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:02.000
They're so good at it

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:05.360
that they can actually pull each
other up through tiny channels,

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:07.680
such as the tiny blood vessels
in your body.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:11.400
That's how oxygen and nutrients
reach the edges of your brain.

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:14.240
The same process,
called capillary action,

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:17.400
allows plants to move water
from deep below the ground

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:20.560
to nourish the leaves and branches
that grow in the sunshine.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:23.720
Our solar system
is drowning in water.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:24.920
Once upon a time,

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:27.920
we thought that we were alone
on Earth with so much water,

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:31.640
but in fact it's the second most
common molecule in the universe.

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:35.080
We now know there's water
on the moon, on Mars, Pluto.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:39.240
In fact there's H2O on almost
every object in our solar system.

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:42.080
And where there's water,
there could be life.

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:45.640
So pour yourself
a glass of water now,

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:48.680
and take a good look at this
colourless, featureless

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:50.520
and tasteless material.

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:52.640
It's actually remarkable.

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:55.320
It breaks so many rules of chemistry

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:57.640
that scientists struggle
to understand it.

00:02:58.080 --> 00:02:59.880
But without its rebel behaviour,

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:02.600
none of us, nor our world,
would exist.

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:07.560
You're only here watching this video
because water is so strange.

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:16.280
Thanks for watching. 
Don’t forget to subscribe! :)

